//? Title: UMAP: inspectable affinities, Iris and Swiss-roll checks
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Visualizing observations with several features requires compressing their
relationships into two coordinates. UMAP builds local affinities before
iterative layout; we inspect those actual weights before using four unscaled
Iris measurements and a known synthetic manifold.
)

\toc

> The method

UMAP uses rho_i equal to the nearest other-point distance and directed weights
exp(−max(0,d_ij−rho_i)/sigma_i) on k neighbors. Sigma is bisected toward a
weight sum log2(k), with64 attempts and a1e−6 floor. Symmetric weights are
v_ij=v(j|i)+v(i|j)−v(j|i)v(i|j). The layout here uses fixed curve1/(1+d²),
processes every edge above1e−4 each epoch, and adds negative-sampled repulsion.
These are explicit simplifications: min_dist is accepted but does not shape the
curve; deterministic weighted edge processing differs from reference UMAP edge
sampling. Dense affinities use O(n²) storage. Duplicate nearest distances can
make the calibration target unattainable.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/umap_iris_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
    d.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{0, 1, 3, 7});
    dm::stats::UMAPOptions o;
    o.n_neighbors = 2;
    o.max_iterations = 1;
    dm::stats::UMAP m(d, {"x"}, o);
    const auto &weights = m.directed_memberships();
    std::print("| source | target | actual directed weight |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
        for (std::size_t j = 0; j < 4; ++j)
            if (i != j)
                std::print("|{}|{}|{}|\n", i, j, weights(i, j));
    dm::dstruct::DataFrame tied;
    tied.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{0, 1, 3, 7, 11, 18});
    dm::stats::UMAPOptions tied_options;
    tied_options.n_neighbors = 3;
    tied_options.max_iterations = 1;
    dm::stats::UMAP tied_model(tied, {"x"}, tied_options);
    double tied_sum = 0;
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < 6; ++j)
        tied_sum += tied_model.directed_memberships()(3, j);
    std::print("\nAt x7 the two nearest distances both equal4: actual sum {}, requested log2(3) {}. This target is unattainable.\n",
               tied_sum, std::log2(3.));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Four raw points0,1,3,7");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, "Actual directed affinity matrix");
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} retained rows", m.observations()));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/umap_iris_tiny.svg");
}
```
